llback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback, which completed. Post-rollback status: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until fixed. The orchestrator partial failure should be investigated."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. Before retrying, I'll check whether it was created so I don't page the on-call engineer twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RkftjiQXPGvig5q9pV3WdK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. The first incident request timed out, so I checked the incident list before anything else. It had been created, so I did not open a duplicate. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n\nThe orchestrator's partial failure during the first rollback attempt should be investigated. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}